      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is actually only needed by the GenerateDefaultGlueCode\u0027s handling of local matrices and the local matrix shader. When we have a GenerateRuntimeGlueCode, we can probably skip that, unless local matrix runtime effects also inline a local matrix (like how gradients and texture shaders do).\n\nCurrently, PaintParams automatically adds a matrix uniform to handle the inverse of the local-to-device transform. It uses that to calculate the local coords for the root effect. That being said, this area is very much in flux and the current solution is mostly a \"get-something-working\" and the eventual plan will be closer to how we can lift local coords to varyings like we do in Ganesh.",
